{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/a2-grammar-pronouns-there-if-as/audio/main-f0fbb5393151.mp3","durationSec":236.496,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":2.68,"text":"A pronoun is a short word that takes the place of a noun."},{"start":3.56,"end":7.98,"text":"We use subject pronouns before the verb, and object pronouns after the verb."},{"start":7.98,"end":12.06,"text":"Subject (before the verb), Object (after the verb)."},{"start":12.06,"end":13.38,"text":"I, me."},{"start":13.58,"end":14.64,"text":"you, you."},{"start":15,"end":15.96,"text":"he, him."},{"start":16.42,"end":17.32,"text":"she, her."},{"start":17.88,"end":18.26,"text":"it, it."},{"start":18.5,"end":19,"text":"we, us."},{"start":19.38,"end":19.78,"text":"they, them."},{"start":20.58,"end":23.08,"text":"Rule 1: Use an object pronoun after a verb."},{"start":23.7,"end":24.26,"text":"I know him."},{"start":24.48,"end":25.24,"text":"(not I know he.)"},{"start":25.96,"end":26.9,"text":"My mother loves me."},{"start":27.24,"end":28.04,"text":"These shoes are nice."},{"start":28.42,"end":29.04,"text":"I want them."},{"start":29.04,"end":34.16,"text":"Rule 2: Use an object pronoun after a preposition (with, for, to, at, and others)."},{"start":34.88,"end":35.78,"text":"I often play with her."},{"start":36.34,"end":37.28,"text":"This present is for you."},{"start":37.6,"end":39.44,"text":"Please listen to us."},{"start":39.9,"end":42.26,"text":"Tip: First think about who the person is."},{"start":42.78,"end":44,"text":"One boy or man is him."},{"start":44.58,"end":46.04,"text":"One girl or woman is her."},{"start":46.68,"end":48.82,"text":"More than one person or thing is them."},{"start":49.4,"end":50.2,"text":"One thing is it."},{"start":50.74,"end":51.5,"text":"My uncle is funny."},{"start":51.68,"end":52.28,"text":"I like him."},{"start":52.82,"end":54.06,"text":"My aunt lives in a big city."},{"start":54.42,"end":55.44,"text":"I visit her every summer."},{"start":55.96,"end":56.78,"text":"I have a new bike."},{"start":57.1,"end":57.98,"text":"I ride it to school."},{"start":57.98,"end":62.58,"text":"We use there is and there are to say that something is in a place."},{"start":62.58,"end":65.86,"text":"Rule 1: Use \"there is\" with one thing."},{"start":66.54,"end":68.66,"text":"Use \"there are\" with two or more things."},{"start":69.24,"end":70.62,"text":"There is a cat on the sofa."},{"start":71.34,"end":72.96,"text":"There are two cats on the sofa."},{"start":73.56,"end":74.58,"text":"There's a clock on the wall."},{"start":75.1,"end":76.2,"text":"(There's = There is)."},{"start":77.18,"end":81.24,"text":"Rule 2: Negative sentences use \"there isn't\" and \"there aren't.\""},{"start":81.72,"end":84.18,"text":"We often use any in negative sentences."},{"start":84.88,"end":86.4,"text":"There isn't a TV in my room."},{"start":86.4,"end":88.6,"text":"There aren't any eggs in the fridge."},{"start":88.6,"end":93.26,"text":"Rule 3: For questions, put \"is\" or \"are\" before \"there.\""},{"start":94,"end":95.26,"text":"Is there a station near here?"},{"start":95.92,"end":96.8,"text":"— Yes, there is."},{"start":96.8,"end":98.14,"text":"/ No, there isn't."},{"start":98.46,"end":99.82,"text":"Are there any books in your bag?"},{"start":100.46,"end":101.2,"text":"— Yes, there are."},{"start":101.64,"end":103.08,"text":"/ No, there aren't."},{"start":104.24,"end":109.28,"text":"Rule 4: To ask about a number, use \"How many + plural noun + are there …?\""},{"start":109.94,"end":111.42,"text":"How many chairs are there in the room?"},{"start":112.02,"end":113,"text":"— There are six chairs."},{"start":113.58,"end":117.42,"text":"Tip: For short answers, use there, not it or they."},{"start":117.64,"end":119.36,"text":"Is there a bus stop on this street?"},{"start":120.36,"end":121.32,"text":"— Yes, there is."},{"start":121.82,"end":122.86,"text":"(not Yes, it is.)"},{"start":123.9,"end":125.56,"text":"We use if to talk about a condition."},{"start":126.38,"end":128.04,"text":"A condition is something that may happen."},{"start":128.66,"end":130.62,"text":"The other part of the sentence tells the result."},{"start":131.52,"end":133.54,"text":"If it is sunny, we will go to the beach."},{"start":134.66,"end":135.98,"text":"Condition: it is sunny."},{"start":136.88,"end":138.6,"text":"Result: we will go to the beach."},{"start":139.36,"end":143.6,"text":"Rule 1: In the \"if\" part, use the present tense, even when you talk about the future."},{"start":144.44,"end":146.44,"text":"If it rains tomorrow, I will stay home."},{"start":147.06,"end":148.36,"text":"(not If it will rain tomorrow …)."},{"start":149,"end":151.02,"text":"If you are free, let's play a game."},{"start":151.66,"end":154.52,"text":"If she gets up early, she will catch the first train."},{"start":154.52,"end":163.02,"text":"Rule 2: The other part often uses \"will,\" \"can,\" or a request like \"please\" or \"let's.\""},{"start":163.02,"end":164.98,"text":"If you finish your homework, you can watch TV."},{"start":165.6,"end":167.92,"text":"If you have a question, please ask me."},{"start":168.52,"end":171.92,"text":"Rule 3: The \"if\" part can come first or second."},{"start":172.7,"end":174.9,"text":"When it comes first, put a comma after it."},{"start":175.2,"end":176.92,"text":"When it comes second, you don't need a comma."},{"start":177.38,"end":178.82,"text":"If you are tired, you can sleep."},{"start":179.48,"end":180.9,"text":"You can sleep if you are tired."},{"start":182.06,"end":187.42,"text":"We use as + adjective + as to say that two people or things are the same in some way."},{"start":188.02,"end":192.18,"text":"Rule 1: Use the basic form of the adjective between \"as\" and \"as.\""},{"start":192.72,"end":195.04,"text":"Don't use the \"-er\" or \"-est\" form."},{"start":195.98,"end":197.78,"text":"My bag is as heavy as your bag."},{"start":198.28,"end":199.4,"text":"(not as heavier as)."},{"start":199.94,"end":201.48,"text":"This room is as big as that room."},{"start":202.06,"end":203.56,"text":"Today is as cold as yesterday."},{"start":204.32,"end":207.4,"text":"Rule 2: You can also use the basic form of an adverb."},{"start":208.08,"end":209.86,"text":"My brother runs as fast as my father."},{"start":210.46,"end":211.9,"text":"I can sing as well as my sister."},{"start":212.64,"end":215.9,"text":"Rule 3: \"Not as … as\" means \"less than.\""},{"start":216.26,"end":218.06,"text":"It shows that two things are not the same."},{"start":218.7,"end":220.22,"text":"My dog is not as big as your dog."},{"start":220.64,"end":221.68,"text":"(Your dog is bigger.)"},{"start":222.6,"end":224.8,"text":"This test is not as difficult as the last test."},{"start":225.36,"end":226.86,"text":"(The last test was more difficult.)"},{"start":227.38,"end":229.44,"text":"Tip: Always use as two times."},{"start":230.08,"end":232.56,"text":"Don't use than with as … as."},{"start":233.06,"end":234.62,"text":"She is as tall as her mother."},{"start":235.2,"end":236.06,"text":"(not as tall than)."}],"words":[{"text":"A","start":0,"end":0.18},{"text":"pronoun","start":0.18,"end":0.5},{"text":"is","start":0.5,"end":0.76},{"text":"a","start":0.76,"end":0.9},{"text":"short","start":0.9,"end":1.1},{"text":"word","start":1.1,"end":1.34},{"text":"that","start":1.34,"end":1.58},{"text":"takes","start":1.58,"end":1.74},{"text":"the","start":1.74,"end":1.96},{"text":"place","start":1.96,"end":2.16},{"text":"of","start":2.16,"end":2.36},{"text":"a","start":2.36,"end":2.46},{"text":"noun","start":2.46,"end":2.68},{"text":"We","start":3.56,"end":3.64},{"text":"use","start":3.64,"end":3.84},{"text":"subject","start":3.84,"end":4.18},{"text":"pronouns","start":4.18,"end":4.64},{"text":"before","start":4.64,"end":4.98},{"text":"the","start":4.98,"end":5.16},{"text":"verb","start":5.16,"end":5.38},{"text":"and","start":5.38,"end":6.14},{"text":"object","start":6.14,"end":6.5},{"text":"pronouns","start":6.5,"end":6.96},{"text":"after